r portraying a superhero  must follow it's to never get your hopes  up you might be the first pick to play a  superhero on a TV series and the last  pick to play a superhero in a feature  film despite wanting to play the flash  in the DCU movie the role of Barry Allen  was recast save and behave if there's  one thing every actor knows all too well  is that job security doesn't exist  unlike some TV shows the cast of the  flash doesn't receive the biggest  paychecks and they're at the mercy of  the showrunners so if they start  misbehaving or acting like total drama  queens they can get written off the show  no matter how important they are to the  plot their roles aren't set in stone and  if they lose their jobs finding a new  gig can be difficult due to them being  typecast saving their paychecks and  treating everyone on the set the way  they want to be treated is the golden  rule don't believe the scrip most of the  time if your character dies in the  script it's time to say goodbye to your  role but that just isn't the case for  the cast of the flash tons of characters  have passed away in the script only to  make  come back in upcoming episodes since the  flash deals with alternate universes  time jumps and doppelgangers the cash  shouldn't believe everything they read  in the script just ask Tom Cavanagh time  to travel the flash is so fast he makes  travelling around the world look like a  total breeze but while Barry Allen only  needs two feet to challenge the speed of  light grant gustin and the rest of the  cast take public transportation just  like the rest of us since the flash is  filmed on location in Vancouver Canada  actors need to be committed to  travelling north of the border to film  the series failing to respect this rule  can result in characters receiving less  screen time or being written off  altogether always be acting actors were  born to put on a show but sometimes it  takes them a little while to realize  that making a fake means acting 